{"step_index":680,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T00:23:37Z","thinking":"**Refining Error Handling**\n\nI've hit a snag. The `replace_file_content` method didn't correctly manage `window.activeProcesses`. However, I'm thinking of completely removing its client-side management because it's too problematic. I need to make some changes to prevent this from causing further errors.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":false,"Description":"Make exitApp check DB for active processes instead of client side variable","EndLine":1082,"Instruction":"Update exitApp to fetch history and check for processing items","ReplacementContent":"// Exit App\nasync function exitApp() {\n    try {\n        let isRunning = false;\n        if (window.pywebview && window.pywebview.api) {\n            const historyStr = await window.pywebview.api.get_history();\n            const history = JSON.parse(historyStr);\n            isRunning = history.some(item => item.status === 'processing');\n        }\n        \n        if (isRunning) {\n            showCustomConfirm('تأكيد الإغلاق', 'توجد عمليات مطابقة قيد التشغيل في الخلفية. هل أنت متأكد من الإغلاق؟', async () => {\n                await window.pywebview.api.exit_app();\n            });\n        } else {\n            if (window.pywebview && window.pywebview.api) {\n                await window.pywebview.api.exit_app();\n            }\n        }\n    } catch (e) {\n        console.error(e);\n        // Fallback\n        if (window.pywebview && window.pywebview.api) {\n            window.pywebview.api.exit_app();\n        }\n    }\n}","StartLine":1078,"TargetContent":"// Exit App\nfunction exitApp() {\n    if (window.activeProcesses > 0) {\n        showCustomConfirm('تأكيد الإغلاق', 'توجد عمليات مطابقة قيد التشغيل في الخلفية. هل أنت متأكد من الإغلاق؟', async () => {\n            try {\n                if (window.pywebview && window.pywebview.api) {\n        