فهو كده هيقرأ هيخليني أحمل الملفات على طول ولا هيبدأ يعمل الفايلات من أول وجديد؟... أنت عامل parsing بس ما فيش extract\" (Addressed via MD5 caching).\n- **On Scrolling:** \"الـ scroll ممنوع الـ scroll... ممكن تخليه pop up يعني ممكن الـ loading والـ بتاع ده يكون pop up\" (Addressed).\n- **On Synchronization:** \"أنا لغيت العمليات اللي قبل كده. طب هو شغال على ايه؟... فكل حاجه تبقى مسمعة ومرتبطة ببعضها.\" (Addressed).\n\n### Context Provided\n- **Screenshot:** Uploaded an image showing the UI displaying a toast error: `the JSON object must be str, bytes or bytearray, not list`.\n\n### API Keys & Credentials\n- **MSEMAX API Key**: `[REDACTED_CREDENTIAL]` (Server at `D:\\AI_Engineer\\MSEMAX\\`)\n- **Unstructured.io API Key**: stored in project `.env` file at `d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\.env`\n\n---\n\n## 3. Work Accomplished\n\n- **Fixed WebView2 COM/UI Thread Crash (Completed):** Discovered that native JS blocking dialogs (`confirm()`) hijack the Windows event pump, causing `pywebview`'s IPC background threads to throw `InvalidCastException` when polling WebView2 properties. Replaced all `confirm()` calls with a custom, non-blocking HTML modal (`#custom-modal`), permanently fixing the fatal \"خطأ في جلب السجل\" and COM errors.\n- **Fixed Scroll & Progress UI (Completed):** Implemented the user's suggestion. Removed `overflow-y: auto` from `.main-content` entirely. Transformed `#progress-area` into a fixed `#progress-modal` overlay with a blur effect so it doesn't push the DOM down or trigger scrollbars during processing.\n- **Fixed App Synchronization & `exitApp` Logic (Completed):** The JS state `window.activeProcesses` was completely de-synchronized if a process was deleted from the history view. `exitApp()` now asynchronously fetches the live SQLite DB state (`get_history()`) and explicitly checks if `status === 'processing'` before warning the user. Also prevented the \"Delete\" button from rendering for running processes.\n- **Added Unstructured API MD5 Caching