{"step_index":722,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T00:33:36Z","thinking":"**Analyzing Data Retrieval**\n\nI've realized a significant detail. The `get_all_processes()` function doesn't actually parse any JSON. It directly returns the data fetched from the database as a list of dictionaries. This means the JSON parsing is likely handled elsewhere, and I need to identify that location for further analysis.\n\n\n**Identifying the Root Cause**\n\nI've hit a major snag! I've realized `get_all_processes` returns raw SQLite rows as dictionaries. The 'shortage_files' field is a TEXT field storing a JSON string. The current deduplication logic in `start_process` is completely broken, because it's sorting the characters of the string instead of the JSON array. This means that a process can never be considered identical, and so the deduplication never works! My immediate priority is fixing `get_all_processes` to deserialize those JSON strings correctly. I also need to evaluate the impact of this change on `index.html`.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":false,"Description":"Fix deduplication check matching string to list","EndLine":17,"Instruction":"Parse JSON strings from the database before sorting and comparing","ReplacementContent":"            # Check for existing process with same files\n            existing_processes = self.db.get_all_processes()\n            for p in existing_processes:\n                try:\n                    db_shortage = json.loads(p.get('shortage_files', '[]'))\n                    db_warehouse = json.loads(p.get('warehouse_files', '[]'))\n                except:\n                    continue\n                    \n                if sorted(db_shortage) == sorted(shortage_filenames) and sorted(db_warehouse) == sorted(warehouse_filenames):\n                    if p.get('status') in ['completed', 'reviewing']:\n                        # It's an identical process that finished\n                        stats = self.db.get_process_stats(p['id'])\n                        return {\"success\": True, \"existing\": True, \"process_id\": p['id'], \"stats\": stats}","StartLine":9,"TargetContent":"            # Check for existing process with same files\n            existing_processes = self.db.get_all_processes()\n            for p in existing_processes:\n                if sorted(p.get('shortage_files', [])) == sorted(shortage_filenames) and sorted(p.get('warehouse_files', [])) == sorted(warehouse_filenames):\n                    if p.get('status') in ['completed', 'reviewing']:\n                        # It's an identical process that finished\n                        stats = self.db.get_process_stats(p['id'])\n                        return {\"success\": True, \"existing\": True, \"process_id\": p['id'], \"stats\": stats}","TargetFile":"d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\desktop_app\\backend.py","toolAction":"Fix JSON parsing in backend","toolSummary":"Fix backend check"}}]}
